<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The hollow mark: "something needs doing" in ink, "no verdict yet" in
    ink-faint — one shape, two states, told apart only by the tint.

    Geometry ported from InkJudgment.ATTENTION / PENDING and WeekMark.OPEN_DOT:
    a ring whose centreline sits at the source's `radius - hairline / 2f`
    (6 - 1.85/2 = 5.075 at stroke 1.85 on viewport 12) — outer edge 6, inner
    edge 4.15.

    Authored as an even-odd FILLED annulus, not a stroked path, on purpose: the
    first device build drew the filled mark and lost this one entirely, and the
    difference between them was exactly stroke-vs-fill. Fill-only geometry rides
    the code path the working mark proves; a stroked ring rides whatever the
    launcher's RemoteViews pipeline makes of vector strokes. Same pixels when
    both work — only one of them always works.

    The authored colour is IRRELEVANT: every use site draws this through
    ColorFilter.tint(ColorProvider), which is how the one-ink rule survives into
    a surface that cannot read LogbookTheme.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="12dp"
    android:height="12dp"
    android:viewportWidth="12"
    android:viewportHeight="12">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#000000"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M6,6 m-6,0 a6,6 0 1,0 12,0 a6,6 0 1,0 -12,0 M6,6 m-4.15,0 a4.15,4.15 0 1,0 8.3,0 a4.15,4.15 0 1,0 -8.3,0" />
</vector>
